Z||000009||onfire||11-10-2000||03:14 PM||||The car was designed by Ed Newton, who worked for Roth Studios. He built it for Roach Inc. in Columbus, Ohio. They say (HotRod mag.) that it cost $100,000 to build in '70's money.It had "fuel injected Ford quad overhead cam Indy car engine and Hewland Transaxle." Its still ugly.<P>------------------<BR>"I know a little bit about everything, and alot about nothing"<BR><A HREF="http://homestead.deja.com/user.on_fire/on_fire.html" TARGET=_blank>Check out my waist of banbwidth.</A>||||reg||1
